{"name":"Homeward Bound","hex":"#e9bf91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"homeward bound","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homeward_bound"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homeward Bound (1923 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Homeward Bound is a 1923 American silent drama film directed by Ralph Ince and written by Peter B. Kyne, Jack Cunningham, and Paul Sloane. The film stars Thomas Meighan, Lila Lee, Charles S. Abbe, William P. Carleton, Hugh Cameron, and Gus Weinberg. The film was released on July 29, 1923, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Homeward_Bound_lobby_card.jpg/330px-Homeward_Bound_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeward_Bound_(1923_film)","wikidata":"Q13460558"},{"title":"Homeward Bound (Simon & Garfunkel song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Homeward Bound\" is a song by the American music duo Simon & Garfunkel, released as a single on January 19, 1966 by Columbia Records. It was written by Paul Simon and produced by Bob Johnston. Simon wrote the song during his time in England, probably while waiting for a train at Widnes railway station, where a plaque commemorates the event."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/60/Homeward_Bound_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeward_Bound_(Simon_%26_Garfunkel_song)","wikidata":"Q1626100"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Widnes_railway_station.jpg/500px-Widnes_railway_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Widnes_railway_station.jpg/1280px-Widnes_railway_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Widnes_railway_station.jpg/500px-Widnes_railway_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Widnes railway station, England, where Simon wrote \"Homeward Bound\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWidnes_railway_station.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Homeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg/500px-Homeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Homeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg/1280px-Homeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Homeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg/500px-Homeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A plaque commemorating the song at Widnes railway station","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeward_Bound_-_widnes_train_station.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Homeward bound (NYPL Hades-464471-1165526)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Homeward_bound_%28NYPL_Hades-464471-1165526%29.jpg/500px-Homeward_bound_%28NYPL_Hades-464471-1165526%29.jpg","ratio":0.7112877583465819,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Homeward_bound_(NYPL_Hades-464471-1165526).jpg","share":0.14625},{"title":"Homeward Bound, Albert Pinkham Ryder, c. 1893-1894, oil on canvas mounted on wood panel - Phillips Collection - DSC04832","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49